AReaL-local extension to /inference/v1/generate. No upstream equivalent.

Adds `expected_token_ids` and refuses to generate unless the fully preprocessed
engine prompt equals it.

RL requires that behavior logprobs and training logprobs come from the same token
sequence. On the multimodal path the caller cannot simply send that sequence:
vLLM treats a tokenized multimodal prompt as unexpanded and expands placeholders
itself, so an already-expanded prompt is expanded a second time. Measured on
Qwen3-VL-2B with one 112x112 image, a 64-placeholder prompt came back with 127.

The contract is therefore inverted: `token_ids` carries one placeholder per media
item and `expected_token_ids` carries the caller's locally expanded prompt. This
check confirms vLLM's expansion agrees with the processor that built the training
row, so a processor-version skew between proxy and server fails the request
instead of silently training on a prompt the model never saw.

Applies on top of vllm.v0.23.0-content-parts.patch, but has a different lifetime:
keep it until upstream exposes an equivalent assertion, including after the
content-parts backport is dropped.

Diagnostics report lengths, the first divergence index, a bounded token window and
media/placeholder counts. They deliberately never echo the full prompt.

Contains no reference to AReaL's pause event: weight-update policy stays in AReaL
source, in the same-path wrapper in areal/engine/vllm_ext/areal_vllm_server.py.

